title: 'statement-store: refresh DHT affinity after peer eviction'

doc:
- audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
  description: |-
    Nodes running with `STATEMENT_STORE_V2_DHT_ENABLED=1` now refresh the statement store's
    DHT-affinity snapshot after evicting a DHT-eligible peer. This prevents removed peers from
    continuing to affect retention decisions. Sweeps that leave the eligible-peer index unchanged
    skip the snapshot copy. Discovery and eviction policies are unchanged, and nodes with the
    v2 DHT path disabled are unaffected.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
